- name: runtime_note
  id: note
  parameters:
    content: 'DEFAULT = SOFTWARE SIMULATION. The graph intentionally runs without a Pluto connected: a generated 800 Hz audio tone is encoded, framed, FEC-coded, QPSK-modulated, pulse-shaped, interpolated to 339.2 kS/s, passed through an AWGN + carrier-offset Channel Model, decimated, synchronized and decoded, then displayed on the RX audio/spectrum/constellation views. Pluto TX and Pluto RX blocks are retained in the graph but DISABLED. Audio Source and Audio Sink are retained but DISABLED. Start with Simulation Noise=0 and Frequency Offset=0. Later enable the Pluto blocks and replace the simulation loopback with the actual RF path for cabled/authorized OTA testing.'
  states:
    bus_sink: false
    bus_source: false
    bus_structure: null
    coordinate: [360, 600]
    rotation: 0
    state: enabled


